+  // to the destination, nor the destination's back. Claiming support would have
+  // QUIC mark packets ECT and then fail its own ECN validation when no counts
+  // came back, which advertises a capability the transport cannot serve.
+  return socket_ && socket_->GetEncapsulation().preserves_ecn;
